{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (Task ID: 5275) from a cobbler-scaffold code generation pipeline. The task is to implement srd025-unexpand requirements R2.1, R2.2, and R2.3 in the go-unix-utils project. These requirements cover the `-a` flag behavior for the `unexpand` command, which converts ALL whitespace (not just leading) to tabs where alignment permits. The task requires:\n   - Modifying `cmd/unexpand/main.go` to ensure R2.1-R2.3 are fully implemented\n   - Adding differential test cases to `cmd/unexpand/unexpand_test.go` covering R2.1-R2.3\n   - Ensuring `go build`, `go vet`, and `go test` all pass\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU unexpand utility reimplementation in Go\n   - Differential testing pattern (comparing Go binary output against GNU reference `gunexpand`)\n   - Tab stop calculation (interval-based and position-list-based)\n   - Space-to-tab conversion: leading-only (default) vs all whitespace (`-a` flag)\n   - `-t` flag implies `-a` mode (per R3.3)\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` framework with `DiffTest` struct, `BuildBinary`, `LC_ALL=C` default\n   - Column-based tab alignment logic\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd025-unexpand.yaml`\n      - Source of truth for requirements. R2.1: `-a` converts all space runs to tabs at every column position. R2.2: single space not reaching tab stop stays as space. R2.3: first non-whitespace char doesn't stop conversion with `-a`.\n      - Key SRD text:\n        ```\n        R2.1: -a must convert all runs of spaces (not just leading) where replacement with tabs aligns to a tab stop. The rule is the same as R1.1 applied at every column position in the line, not only at the start.\n        R2.2: A single space that does not reach a tab stop must be kept as a space even with -a.\n        R2.3: The first non-space, non-tab character on the line does not stop the conversion; -a processes the entire line.\n        ```\n   \n   - `cmd/unexpand/main.go` (EXISTING - full file read, 211 lines)\n      - Already has R1.1-R1.4 implemented. The `-a` flag is already parsed and `allMode` variable is used in the `unexpand()` function. The core logic in `unexpand()` already checks `leading || allMode` for space and tab handling, so R2.1-R2.3 may already be substantially implemented.\n      - Key function signatures and structures:\n        ```go\n        type tabStops struct { interval int; positions []int }\n        func parseArgs(args []string) (tabStops, bool, []string, error)\n        func parseTabStops(val string) (tabStops, error)\n        func unexpand(r io.Reader, w *bufio.Writer, stops tabStops, allMode bool)\n        func nextTabStop(col int, stops tabStops) int\n        func emitCompacted(w *bufio.Writer, startCol int, count int, stops tabStops)\n        ```\n      - The `unexpand()` function's space handling (lines 143-153): when `leading || allMode`, spaces are accumulated in `spaceRun`; otherwise written directly. This already enables `-a` mode processing.\n      - The `default` case (lines 174-180): flushes spaceRun via `emitCompacted`, writes byte, sets `leading = false`. After this, in allMode, subsequent spaces will still be accumulated because `allMode` is checked.\n   \n   - `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (full file read, 240 lines)\n      - Provides `DiffTest` struct, `RunDiffTests()`, `BuildBinary()`, `ComposeNormalizers()`, `TimestampNormalizer`\n      - `DiffTest` struct: `Name`, `Args`, `Stdin`, `Env`, `WorkDir`, `ExitCode`, `Normalize`, `ExpectedFiles`\n      - `buildEnv()` automatically sets `LC_ALL=C`\n   \n   - `cmd/unexpand/unexpand_test.go` - NOT YET READ. This file needs to be read to understand existing tests before adding new ones.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Implementation has not started.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Initial analysis suggests the existing `cmd/unexpand/main.go` implementation may already handle `-a` mode correctly because the `allMode` variable is already wired into the `unexpand()` function's space/tab handling logic. Need to verify edge cases and add test coverage.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Extremely detailed task specification including role description, repository file list, project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, requirement states), execution constitution, go style constitution, task description with required reading/files/requirements/design decisions/acceptance criteria, shared protocols, and package contracts. The core request is: implement srd025-unexpand R2.1-R2.3 and add tests.\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - Requesting a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Read `cmd/unexpand/unexpand_test.go` to understand existing test structure\n   - Verify that the existing `cmd/unexpand/main.go` implementation correctly handles R2.1-R2.3 (the `-a` flag logic appears already implemented but needs verification)\n   - Add differential test cases for R2.1-R2.3 to `cmd/unexpand/unexpand_test.go`\n   - Run `go build -o bin/unexpand ./cmd/unexpand/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/unexpand/` to check for issues\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/unexpand/ -count=1` to verify tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the three source files (SRD, main.go, difftest.go) and was about to read `cmd/unexpand/unexpand_test.go` (the existing test file) before beginning implementation. I had not yet made any code changes. The analysis shows the `-a` mode logic already exists in `main.go` - the key remaining work is adding test cases and verifying correctness.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Read `cmd/unexpand/unexpand_test.go` to understand the existing test structure, then add differential test cases for R2.1-R2.3. The tests should cover:\n   - R2.1: `-a` converting non-leading spaces to tabs (e.g., `\"a        b\"` with `-a` should produce `\"a\\tb\"`)\n   - R2.2: Single space not reaching tab stop stays as space with `-a`\n   - R2.3: Conversion continues past non-whitespace characters with `-a`\n   \n   From the task description: \"Implement srd025-unexpand requirement R2.1 exactly as specified in the SRD\", \"Implement srd025-unexpand requirement R2.2 exactly as specified in the SRD\", \"Implement srd025-unexpand requirement R2.3 exactly as specified in the SRD\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5275/5f47d362-1ee2-48b5-872f-e8f3954a5278.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f47d362-1ee2-48b5-872f-e8f3954a5278","uuid":"84181cd7-cd59-4161-a2b0-bcb659f43dbf","timestamp":"2026-05-15T14:39:24.950Z","isSynthetic":true}
