{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_013KHbgJSQYwkC4xeQFVmNff","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 26 tests pass. Here's a summary of what changed:\n\n**`cmd/unexpand/main.go`**: Fixed a bug where a single non-leading space at a tab stop boundary was incorrectly converted to a tab. GNU unexpand requires 2+ spaces for non-leading tab conversion (per G3/R2.2). Added a `flush` closure in `unexpand()` that checks `!leading && spaceRun < 2` and emits raw spaces instead of calling `emitCompacted` in that case.\n\n**`cmd/unexpand/unexpand_test.go`** (new): Created differential test file with 26 test cases covering:\n- R1.1–R1.4: 8 tests for default leading-only behavior\n- R2.1: 7 tests for `-a` converting non-leading space runs to tabs\n- R2.2: 4 tests for single/short space runs staying as spaces with `-a`\n- R2.3: 7 tests verifying `-a` processes entire lines past non-whitespace characters"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1273,"cache_read_input_tokens":40999,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1273},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f47d362-1ee2-48b5-872f-e8f3954a5278","uuid":"e2bf6f54-2049-49ea-9651-0e959fedf773"}
